  description: Mars is the fourth planet from the Sun and is often called the Red
    Planet because iron minerals in its soil give it a reddish appearance. It has
    enormous volcanoes, deep valleys, polar ice caps, and evidence that liquid water
    once flowed across its surface.
  interestingFact: Mars is home to Olympus Mons, the largest known volcano in the
    Solar System, standing approximately 22 kilometers tall.
